{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BpDJFpdc6D581tLsGwkPPb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, the directory exists. Now let me write the full LaTeX paper. I need to carefully organize the data from the experiment_data.json and paper_framing.md into a coherent paper.\n\nLet me plan the paper structure:\n\n1. Abstract\n2. Introduction\n3. Related Work\n4. Method (dataset construction, trace representations, VOTA, SFT setup)\n5. Experiments\n   - Main results (Table 1: 3×4 cross-model matrix)\n   - Information density analysis (Table 2: full_trace → VOTA → exception_only gradient on 1.5B)\n   - Cross-model exception dominance (Table 3)\n   - Marker ablation (Table 4)\n   - Seed robustness (Table 5: loop_only 3-seed)\n   - Tier comparison (Table 6)\n   - Appendix: CodeLlama-13B\n6. Discussion\n7. Conclusion\n\nNow I'm pulling the key experimental results from the data—Qwen-1.5B achieves 91% with VOTA but drops to 73.3% with full traces, and the exception-only variant without markers reaches 97%, showing how trace granularity and marker presence significantly impact performance across the different model configurations. Now I'm pulling the core results from the three main models—Qwen-7B, DeepSeek-6.7B, and Qwen-1.5B—along with their calibration metrics to structure the paper's findings. Looking at the performance metrics across different model configurations and ablations. The CodeLlama results show full_trace at 75.5% with exception_only reaching 99.7%, and VOTA performing strongly at 95.5%. For the Qwen-7B ablations, removing the nomarker component drops performance by about 2.9 percentage points on average, while the loop-only variant achieves 85.4% accuracy. Now I'm ready to structure the paper following the narrative framework and start drafting the title and introduction. Now I'm mapping each experiment from the data file to its corresponding table and section—the main results matrix will anchor the cross-model comparison, while the information density and ablation studies will break down what's driving the performance gains. I need to make sure the marker ablation and seed robustness experiments are properly accounted for, and I'll include the CodeLlama validation in the appendix.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":210,"cache_read_input_tokens":45060,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":210},"output_tokens":11,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0130045c-2d16-484c-849f-d0660534f6f1","uuid":"efd3b91b-65c0-40d8-be75-d7112ad4ed21"}
